ber": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d03", "start": 514, "end": 578, "text": "Bestowal of the Cross of Liberty was terminated on 19 June 1925."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 0, "end": 44, "text": "a vice-chancellor and at least four members."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 45, "end": 128, "text": "The orders of the White Rose of Finland and the Lion of Finland have a joint board."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 129, "end": 226, "text": "The Order of the Cross of Liberty was founded on March 4, 1918, upon the initiative of General C."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 227, "end": 229, "text": "G."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 230, "end": 232, "text": "E."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 233, "end": 244, "text": "Mannerheim."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 245, "end": 352, "text": "The Finnish artist Akseli Gallen-Kallela was commissioned to design the Order's insignia with the swastika."}, "D5S8": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 353, "end": 491, "text": "At its foundation there were seven classes: grand cross, cross of liberty (1st to 4th class) and the medal of liberty (1st and 2nd class)."}, "D5S9": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d04", "start": 492, "end": 574, "text": "The decorations of the Order of the Cross of Liberty were initially conferred only"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0229-dba0cad86a23:d00:c0", "entity": "Cross of Liberty", "scope": "Estonia", "claim": "The Cross of Liberty was established on 24 February 1919 by then Prime Minister of Estonia, Kon